{
  "_comment": "baitbook i2i: FLUX.2 [klein] (4B or 9B) native reference editing. The Angler fills in the model files (GGUF or safetensors: it picks the loaders), prompt, source image, size, steps, cfg and seed from baitbook.toml before queueing. Decoding is tiled by default: on Windows HIP a single multi-GB VAE allocation can fail while the language model is resident. The source goes up to ComfyUI's temp folder and the result comes back through PreviewImage, which writes there too: ComfyUI empties it each time it starts, so no copies pile up in its input or output folders.",
  "1": {
    "class_type": "UNETLoader",
    "inputs": {
      "unet_name": "flux-2-klein-4b.safetensors",
      "weight_dtype": "default"
    }
  },
  "2": {
